WEBVTT

NOTE Captions match the narration. Times follow the spoken words.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.172
Every AI agent.

2
00:00:02.172 --> 00:00:04.200
One workspace you own.

3
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.320
In a project, you give
the coordinator a goal.

4
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.920
It starts a worker for each part
and lists them in the Threads rail.

5
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.600
Each job gets the model that fits.

6
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:25.200
Here Codex writes tip.py while
Claude writes the README.

7
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.757
Results come back to one conversation.

8
00:00:27.757 --> 00:00:31.200
The coordinator checks each
worker's output against the goal.

9
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.320
Hit a limit?

10
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.040
SpecWithCode shows every account's limits.

11
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:43.240
When Claude runs out, Continue with
Codex carries the conversation over,

12
00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:47.120
so Codex knows the word
only Claude was told.

13
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.040
One record in git.

14
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:55.920
The open-source CLI hands off at
90%, and any agent picks it up.

15
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.840
Bring your agents.

16
00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.680
Keep your machines.
